# Bible local-data fix for VS Code

This patch updates both Bible implementations so KJV, ASV, and AMP chapter data and word search use the bundled JSON files rather than Supabase or `/bible/*.json` URL requests.

## Files required

The following files must already exist in the repository:

- `public/bible/kjv.json`
- `public/bible/asv.json`
- `public/bible/amp.json`
- `app/bible/page.tsx`
- `public/bible/bible_page.tsx`

## Apply the patch in VS Code

1. Open the repository folder in VS Code.
2. Copy `counselling-bible-local.patch` into the repository root.
3. Open the VS Code terminal and run:

```bash
git apply counselling-bible-local.patch
```

4. Verify the changes:

```bash
npx tsc --noEmit
git diff --check
```

## Core code added to both Bible components

```tsx
import kjvData from "@/public/bible/kjv.json";
import asvData from "@/public/bible/asv.json";
import ampData from "@/public/bible/amp.json";

type BibleData = Record<string, Record<string, { v: number; t: string }[]>>;

const LOCAL_BIBLE_DATA: Record<Version, BibleData> = {
  kjv: kjvData as BibleData,
  asv: asvData as BibleData,
  amp: ampData as BibleData,
};
```

## Chapter loading used by the active route

In `app/bible/page.tsx`, the chapter effect should read from `LOCAL_BIBLE_DATA` like this:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  setChapterLoading(true);
  setChapterError(null);
  setHighlightedVerse(null);
  setNote("");

  try {
    const rawVerses = LOCAL_BIBLE_DATA[version]?.[book]?.[String(chapterNum)];
    if (!rawVerses || rawVerses.length === 0) {
      throw new Error("Chapter not found in bundled Bible data.");
    }

    const verses: BibleVerse[] = rawVerses.map((verse, index) => ({
      id: index,
      book,
      chapter: chapterNum,
      verse: verse.v,
      text: verse.t,
    }));

    setChapter({ book_name: book, chapter: chapterNum, verses });
  } catch (err: unknown) {
    const message = err instanceof Error ? err.message : "Failed to load chapter.";
    setChapterError(message);
    setChapter(null);
  } finally {
    setChapterLoading(false);
  }
}, [book, chapterNum, version]);
```

## Local word search

The active route should search the selected bundled data instead of calling `.from("bible_verses")`:

```tsx
const searchBible = async () => {
  if (!searchWord.trim()) return;
  setSearchLoading(true);
  setSearchResults([]);

  try {
    const word = searchWord.trim().toLowerCase();
    const results: BibleVerse[] = [];
    const bibleData = LOCAL_BIBLE_DATA[version];

    for (const [bookName, chapters] of Object.entries(bibleData)) {
      for (const [chapter, verses] of Object.entries(chapters)) {
        for (const verse of verses) {
          if (verse.t.toLowerCase().includes(word)) {
            results.push({
              id: results.length,
              book: bookName,
              chapter: Number(chapter),
              verse: verse.v,
              text: verse.t,
            });
          }
        }
      }
    }

    setSearchResults(results);
  } finally {
    setSearchLoading(false);
  }
};
```

Supabase can remain imported for saving favorites and devotional notes. It is no longer used for reading Bible chapters or searching Bible text.
